          },
          "notes": [
            {
              "chapter": 1,
              "v_start": 1,
              "v_end": 1,
              "text": "The burden — The prophet seems to speak of these grievous things, as a burden which he himself groaned under."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 1,
              "v_start": 4,
              "v_end": 4,
              "text": "Therefore — Because the wicked go on with impunity. The law - The whole law, moral, ceremonial, and judicial. Is slacked - Is slighted, and not observed. Go forth - From magistrates, Judges, and public officers. Doth compass about - As it were besieges, with design to oppress and ruin."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "role": "psalm",
          "ref": "Psalm 119:137-144",
          "refKey": "Ps.119.137-Ps.119.144",
          "tags": {
            "theme": [
              "faithfulness",
              "justice",
              "law-and-commandment",
              "word-of-god"
            ],
            "mood": [
              "trust"
            ],
            "function": [
              "illumination-word"
            ]
          },
          "notes": [
            {
              "chapter": 119,
              "v_start": 140,
              "v_end": 140,
              "text": "Pure — Without the least mixture of falsehood."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 119,
              "v_start": 142,
              "v_end": 142,
              "text": "Everlasting — The same in all ages and places."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 119,
              "v_start": 143,
              "v_end": 143,
              "text": "Trouble — Outward troubles and anguish of spirit."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "role": "second",
          "ref": "2 Thessalonians 1:1-4, 11-12",
          "refKey": "2Thess.1.1-2Thess.1.4",
          "tags": {
            "theme": [
              "faith-and-trust",
              "judgment",
              "suffering-and-endurance",
              "thanksgiving"
            ],
            "mood": [
              "assurance",
              "exhortation"
            ]
          },
          "notes": [
            {
              "chapter": 1,
              "v_start": 1,
              "v_end": 1,
              "text": "Congratulates their constancy in the faith, and exhorts them to advance daily in grace and wisdom."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 1,
              "v_start": 2,
              "v_end": 2,
              "text": "Reforms their mistake concerning the coming of our Lord And,"
            },
            {
              "chapter": 1,
              "v_start": 3,
              "v_end": 3,
              "text": "Recommends several Christian duties. The parts of it are five: I. The inscription, Chap. i. 1, 2 II. Thanksgiving and prayer for them, 3-12 III. The doctrine concerning the man of sin,. ii. 1-12 Whence he comforts them against this trial, 13, 14 Adding exhortation and prayer, 15-17 IV. An exhortation to prayer, with a prayer for. iii. 1-5 them, to correct the disorderly, 6-16 V. The conclusion, 17, 18 2nd THESSALONIANS"
            },
            {
              "chapter": 1,
              "v_start": 4,
              "v_end": 4,
              "text": "Which ye endure — \"That ye may be accounted worthy of the kingdom.\""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "role": "gospel",
          "ref": "Luke 19:1-10",
          "refKey": "Luke.19.1-Luke.19.10",
          "tags": {
            "theme": [
              "deliverance",
              "grace",
              "repentance",
              "wealth-and-possessions"
            ],
            "mood": [
              "joy"
            ],
            "function": [
              "pardon-assurance"
            ]
          },
          "notes": [
            {
              "chapter": 19,
              "v_start": 1,
              "v_end": 1,
              "text": "He passed through Jericho — So that Zacchaeus must have lived near the end of the town: the tree was in the town itself. And he was rich - These words seem to refer to the discourse in the last chapter, ver. 24, particularly to ver. 27. Zacchiaeus is a proof, that it is possible by the power of God for even a rich man to enter into the kingdom of heaven."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 19,
              "v_start": 2,
              "v_end": 2,
              "text": "The chief of the publicans — What we would term, commissioner of the customs. A very honourable as well as profitable place."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 19,
              "v_start": 4,
              "v_end": 4,
              "text": "And running before — With great earnestness. He climbed up - Notwithstanding his quality: desire conquering honour and shame."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 19,
              "v_start": 5,
              "v_end": 5,
              "text": "Jesus said, Zacchaeus, make haste and come down — What a strange mixture of passions must Zacchaeus have now felt, hearing one speak, as knowing both his name and his heart!"
            },
            {
              "chapter": 19,
              "v_start": 7,
              "v_end": 7,
              "text": "They all murmured — All who were near: though most of them rather out of surprise than indignation."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 19,
              "v_start": 8,
              "v_end": 8,
              "text": "And Zacchaeus stood — Showing by his posture, his deliberate, purpose and ready mind, and said, Behold, Lord, I give - I determine to do it immediately."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 19,
              "v_start": 9,
              "v_end": 9,
              "text": "He also is a son of Abraham — A Jew born, and as such has a right to the first offer of salvation."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 19,
              "v_start": 10,
              "v_end": 10,
              "text": "Matt. xviii, 11."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
